I'm using the writing-plans skill to create the implementation plan. Per your standing preference (no committed planning docs), I'll write the plan inline in this response rather than to `docs/superpowers/plans/...`. If you want a saved copy later, just ask.

# Review TUI viewport drill-in Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** Use the checkbox syntax to track progress as you go. Each step is 2–5 minutes. TDD throughout — test first, watch fail, implement, watch pass, commit.

**Goal:** Replace the manual one-line-per-event scrolling in `tui_detail.go` with a `bubbles/v2/viewport` widget that wraps long events and supports standard pager navigation. Keep Ctrl+O usable after both agents finish (instead of quitting the TUI on any key).

**Architecture:** Viewport widget owns scroll state and key bindings. Events are pre-rendered into a long string with wrapped lines, passed to `viewport.SetContent`. Auto-tail via `viewport.AtBottom()`. Post-finish handler changes from "any key quits" to "specific quit keys only."

**Tech Stack:** Go, bubbletea v2, bubbles/v2/viewport (already in deps via `cmd/entire/cli/activity_tui.go`), `github.com/charmbracelet/x/ansi` (already in deps via `tui_text.go`).

**Branch:** `feat/review-detail-viewport` off current `main`. Independent of #1167 and #1175 — both touch different code regions; conflicts at merge are likely minimal and additive.

